{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521290-is-it-confirmed-that-malkav-arkiel-are-actual-siblings-from-the-same-mortal-family","id":1521290,"title":"Is it confirmed that Malkav & Arkiel are actual siblings from the same mortal family?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-23T15:49:26-07:00","id":1521290,"title":"Is it confirmed that Malkav & Arkiel are actual siblings from the same mortal family?","content":"I remember coming across it on wikepedia or other sites if I recall correctly. Has this ever been confirmed by any of the old sourcebooks to your knowledge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T23:01:03-07:00","id":1521318,"title":"","content":"[Forum ate it]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 08-25-2023, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T00:42:02-07:00","id":1521320,"title":"","content":"Okay, I HATE the Forum's span-filter flagging system<br /> Let's try again<br /> I wil ldelete the original<br /> Or not, whatever<br /> So, to answer to your question:<br /> <br /> Yes<br /> I mean, in lot of sourcbooks, including Clanbooks, not just one, it is &quot;confirmed&quot; Malkvas was the twin brother of Arikel.<br /> But from there it went a bit downhill so to speak and things became... complicated<br /> Some scriptures (Beckett's Jyhad Diary, Gehenna and in \u200bThe Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra) claim he had a twin sister, Malakai, Black Hand scriptures say Malakai is imprisoned deep within the Shadowlands because she is so mad and powerful that she warps reality around her. (Malakai is mentioned in the Shaal Fragment as an antediluvian who seeks &quot;peace&quot; during the first Gehenna. However, since Arikel is said to seek unity, the peace Malakai seeks may not be diplomatic in nature. Rather, she could have sought peace by journeying to the Shadowlands or entering Torpor.)<br /> Chaining the Beast mentions one branch of the Path of Lilith, the Path of Awakening. The followers of it believes that Arikel and Malkav were twins, children of Lilith, and that they had a younger sister, Nahema, who also received the Embrace. According to legend, Nahema descended into Hell, but never lost touch with her siblings, her spirit forever bound to them and their childer \u2013 it is Nahema's spirit that whispers in the Malkavian Madness Network, that burns in the hearts of the Toreador. Some of her worshippers call her the Dark Muse, the Anti-Muse, and the Demon Queen of Madness, and she is said to be patron saint of serial killers and torturers<br /> So, puting these together, we have a nice family\u200b<br /> Set, &quot;the Snake&quot; (who may or may not be Sutekh the founder of the Followers of Set and who cut and ate the heart of Arikel aling with Absimiliard - probably a seperate entinty) and Saulot protryed as brothers to the triplets Malakai, Malkav and Arikel<br /> Beckett's Jyhad Diary is the last info about Arikel; Beckett, deep within a pit under a ruins in Ketef Hinnom lost himself to the madness afflicting the Malkavians. While affected he said and wrote the following quotes: &quot;Malkav. Malakai. Arikel. Lilith. Children and mother. Mekhet is free and Malakai follows\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> So, the &quot;family tree&quot; (possibly), by sourcebooks:<br /> Lilith + unknonw father<br /> Malakai, Malkav, Arikel (as triplets)<br /> Set and Saulot (brothers, <i>also</i> the brothers of Malakai, Malkav, Arikel)<br /> Nahema, the youngest sister of the above five, who descended into Hell (not unlike how Ravana became a Yama King in Yomi, I might add) to be the Demon Queen of Madness<br /> <br /> Interesting say the least, yet... in a strange way it is fitting<br /> There is a &quot;patern&quot;<br /> Clanbook: Malkavian Revised suggests that even before the Embrace Malkav was special, possibly an angel or similar to it<br /> Malakai was so mad and powerful she warped reality around her.<br /> Arikel work inspired such emotions within the audience that they had inspired in the mortal population. Caine was deeply touched by it and called Arikel (and Troile) to his side, forgiving them past trespasses; but According Clan Book: Baali, among his brethren, Nergal was the one most adept at dealing with other Cainites. It is said that he served as Arikel's wench, debated philosophy with Troile and traded vice secrets with the Tzimisce Antediluvian. Her &quot;canon&quot; line consist:<br /> - Amarantha (who was mistakenly diablerized by an Assamite judge while he was administering punishment to her. Amarantha's name is one of the possible sources of the word amaranth, the traditional word for diablerie. After her death, there was a cult named the Amaranthan started by her childer as revenge by diablerizing the said same Assamite judge. Her descendants still practice their activities and belief to hunt and devour Diablerists.- more about her in Clanbook: Assamite Revised, and Children of The Blood, Cults of the Blood Gods)<br /> - Mi-ka-il (aka. Beshter aka. the Archangel of Constantinople, Michael) - Who went batshit crazy, and ended up eaten by a Baali, his ex-lover (tho' it is suggested, he pulled a Mithras on her; or in older books, she became a Demon by her own right. Tho' both could be true)<br /> - Iontius aka. Derrick Zeel (an ancient Toreador methusela who somehow gained the ability to feed off his victims through sex rather than by normal vampiric means. - more about him in Clanbook: Toreador, Encyclopaedia Vampirica, Beckett's Jyhad Diary, and DAV: France by Night)<br /> - Minos (the sire of Helena. He was diablerised by his childe) Yezidian refugees from the remains of the Aral Sea refer to the force of ontological evil as &quot;Minos, who is the son of Arikel&quot;, who rests deep within the salt flats of the dried out sea. Minos got eaten by Helena, The Betrayer of Carthage who may or may not an Ifernalist, but her Child, Melinda Galbraith went neck deep in darkness and became the servant of Nergal/ Huitzilopochtli<br /> Nahema descended into Hell to be the Demon Queen of Madness<br /> And Saulot? His whole trip to the East, learning Dharma, bacoming a Demon-Tiger aspirant, and sired the Baali, and ultimately wanted to become the Demon Emperor of the Sixth Age... need I say more?<br /> In my opinion the father <i>wasn't</i> Lucifer - Lilith and Lucifer traveled to the edge of the Endless Sea, where they founded D'hainu, the Garden of Renewal. There she bore six children: three boys \u2014 Kessep (Silver), Shotheq (Silence), and Nesher (Eagle) \u2014 and three girls \u2014 Mem (Water), Oreb (Raven), and Laylah (Night). [even tho' they are three brother and three sister too...)- but someone or <i>something</i> else... After all small group of Jewish djinn called the shedim that have returned to the High Umbra, after their long exile to the physical world, where they traditionally lived in abandoned buildings in Orthodox neighborhoods, trace their lineage to Lilith, and consider her their queen (&quot;malkah ha-shedim&quot; is one of Lilith's traditional titles in Jewish folklore).<br /> And these six siblings displayed quite a few, dare I say <i>Nephilim-like traits and in one way or another had a strong connection to reality warping and with Hell.</i><br /> Who knows, maybe Lucifer is their Father, could be a fun theory to explore.<br /> Or simply after Adam tried to force himself onto her - after spending nights with animals - she was repulsed and used Jehovah's True Name, who helped her and they had an affair; Lilith from there always carried the seed of Jehovah inside her - she became the Mother of Monsters and Demons<br /> But most of these are just fun theories<br /> Back to your original question... ?<br /> Yes<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 08-24-2023, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T09:02:48-07:00","id":1521330,"title":"","content":"Your right it's quite complicated about how source material can get so convulted as time passes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T18:17:47-07:00","id":1521359,"title":"","content":"I think there was an implied canonical backstory in the early editions with actual facts behind them, at least in the minds of the original creators. However, as the original founders of the company and developers of the game lines left, and new people came on board, there were lots of changes for various reasons. There isn't actually one canon any longer. There are more like three or five, and with each new edition the backstory becomes incoherent as contradictory, supplementary, and intentionally false lore are introduced. In my own opinion, while there is some neat stuff in Revised and later editions that I find useful, wherever there is contradiction, retroactive continuity changes, or other disputes, I usually find the earlier lore more compelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-26T13:05:27-07:00","id":1521440,"title":"","content":"Which is why I try to keep things fairly simple in our games such as the 3rd generation just being regular humans in their time and mythic retelling of there origins getting more mythic in scope Mr. Black Fox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T00:06:00-07:00","id":1521452,"title":"","content":"[Forum ate it]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 08-28-2023, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T00:07:34-07:00","id":1521453,"title":"","content":"Oh the lovely flagging on the morning...<br /> It would be too much to ask ,to tone down the sensitivity this trice cursed spam-filter???<br /> Anyhow, one more time:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521290-is-it-confirmed-that-malkav-arkiel-are-actual-siblings-from-the-same-mortal-family?p=1521440#post1521440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the 3rd generation just being regular humans in their time.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is more or less true<br /> I mean, if you following the materials:<br /> Legend has it that <b>Ennoia</b> and <b>Churka</b> were siblings (twins of a god who had many children) or Ennoia was a simple mortal woman, a member of a Cult of Lilith (just like Lamia after her many many years ago) and lover of Ravnos (the 2nd generation children of Caine), but both were simple mortals<br /> <b>The Eldest</b>, the Antediluvian of the Tzimisce was a human, a Mage<br /> <b>Cappadocius</b> while he was a mortal named Sargon was a mortal priest and man of faith, a Seer of great wisdom a bit of Nostredamus of his time, who had his own dealings with the dead, a conversation here and there with spirits of those gone, and he had made several enemies in his time - When the Antediluvian died briefly during the Embrace, those spirits were waiting for him in the lands Beneath, and they attempted to cling to him, to prevent him from returning to his body when the curse of Caine took hold. It is said that, to some extent, they succeeded. Part of Cappadocius never returned from the underworld. Much of his knowledge and self-awareness were lost in that faulty Embrace, and the being who returned was not quite he who began the journey. Cappadocius' very soul had been fragmented, and that is why he harbored such a fascination for the dead: Even when he himself did not realize it, he was constantly seeking the missing portions of himself (this flawed Embrace is also the reason for Cappadocius' deathly appearance; because the spirit that returned to his body was incomplete, it was unable to fully stave off the decay of the grave. It may also be the reason that Augustus Giovanni could not devour his soul completely, as a part of it had always been in the Underworld) He even forgot his name and whenever he was asked about his origins, he would only say that he was &quot;from Cappadocia&quot; hance his moniker, Cappadocius<br /> According to most Ventrue accounts of their founder's origins, Caine saw the potential <b>Veddartha</b> when he was still a youth and took him in, raising him as his own and eventually giving him to Enoch for his Embrace. Legends also tell, he was a foreign nobleman who received the Embrace from Enoch without Caine's guidance. The two not mutually exclusive.<br /> <b>Saulot </b>was a young man with prophetic gifts, a shepperd who reminded Cain of Able<br /> The Lasombra describe their forefather's mortal life as &quot;unremarkable&quot;, that he was a pathetic failure, Embraced for some trivial reason, who flourished unexpectedly.<br /> In one legend <b>Sutekh</b> was a great hunter and warrior whose only rival was his elder brother, Asar (Osiris). They were the grandchildren of Ra, a mighty chieftain who had conquered the people of the Nile, thus uniting Upper and Lower Egypt, forbidden sons of Geb and Nut (whom Ra executed for having children against his wishes, beacause he felt threatened by royal bloodlines and commanded that they must not bear children.)<br /> <b>Absimiliard</b> was an expert and stealthy hunter who hunted sabertooth tigers and whose skill at predation inflamed the dead heart Zillah. She chased and Embraced him, although in the ensuing struggle she also scarred him lightly. A creature of prodigious vanity, this trivial marring of his otherwise perfect looks drove him to obsession, and Absimiliard conceived to murder his sire (as a side note, <b>Lucian </b>in Gehenna is a supernaturally handsome man who effectively leads the Apostates under Lilith. It is suggested that he is in some way related to the Nosferatu: he may have shared a mortal parent or Second Generation sire with Absimiliard and he may be the true Antediluvian of the Nosferatu but probably sired the Guruhi Legacy of the Laibon)<br /> <b>Mekhet</b> in Gehenna was a potent pre-Egyptian blood magician whose body resembles that of a mummified Samedi, Assamite lore states that Mekhet was a great liar. According to the Tzimisce Clan, Mekhet was a sibling of the Eldest (but this could mean he was the childe of Ynosh/Enoch) who, with the Brujah Antediluvian, &quot;played shadow games with mortals, delighting in their own cunning and agendas&quot;.<br /> <b>Haqim </b>was a warrior-hunter who migrated with the herds, had dedicated himself to scholarship during his travels. He learned to read, write and speak the language of the dead. Or was the lord of the armies of the First City who served under the King and Queen of En'esh (other name of the First City, named after their son, En'esh. According to the Toreador Katherine of Montpellier, the &quot;First City&quot; was originally known as Ubar, meaning &quot;Queen of Frankincense.&quot;), Khe-duk and Lianda.<br /> <b>Torile</b> was a fiery youth of great passion while his Sire, <b>Ilyes </b>was a scholar<br /> <br /> To be fair, the deification of the Antediluvan was something that most of the cases never happened, some of them, like Zapatashura and Sutekh were treated as Gods from the begining, the most of the time the Clans not treated their founder as gods - just very dangerous and powerfull ancestors akin to gods.<br /> Trivial difference but a difference non the less<br /> Mortals on the other hand had the habit of worshiping Cainities, but most of the time 4th or 5th generation Methuselah, like Medon, the Ventrue methuselah that set himself as a god-king on an isle in the Aegean, Artemis, his broodmate, Mithras, Arakur and Tiamat - the Ventrue posed as Gods more than anyone else<br /> But there are the Malkavian Louhi, the Tzimisce Byelobog or Kartarirya who tried impersonating Kartikeya, the god of war, only to discover the Brahmans wielded their True Faith as a weapon and saw through such artifice. Surprisingly, in its search to find worshipers among the growing Vedic pantheon, Kartarirya came to understand and appreciate their religion.<br /> The Gangrel Odin (or Einherjar if you treat them as a seperate breed of vampires, descendants of the warrior Canarl), Gilgamesh or Enkidu<br /> Ishtar posed as a goddes and her lover/child Tammuz likewise<br /> Arikel's child, Apollo... well you have guessed it, like his other child, Mi-ka-il, who played the role of the Archangel Michael<br /> The Baali Moloch and Nergal/Huitzilopochtli also liked to play gods<br /> <br /> Many Methuselah were worshiped as Gods... but Antediluvians?<br /> Four or five at best; Zapatashura, Ishtar, Ennoia sometimes as the Tiger Queen, but not really, the Lasombra Antediluvian who commanded the Hyksos and the Sea People against his relatives progenies, and considered a &quot;dark god&quot;...<br /> But the only one who was believed and to this very day is treated as one...?<br /> That one is Sutekh who is a God both by his mortal and immortal followers\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T15:11:15-07:00","id":1521544,"title":"","content":"Sorry to hear that your posts are having trouble Shadowprowler. I hope that you don't have such problems again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value